WEBVTT

01:10.320 --> 01:11.529
You're an asshole.

01:12.655 --> 01:13.782
I didn't need to.

01:19.954 --> 01:21.623
I think we should cancel the wedding.

01:35.887 --> 01:37.013
Okay.

01:38.139 --> 01:39.224
"Okay"?

01:42.227 --> 01:43.895
Did you really just say "okay"?

01:45.522 --> 01:48.108
I don't have anything else to say.

01:49.609 --> 01:50.610
"Okay"?

01:52.195 --> 01:53.238
"Okay"?

01:54.864 --> 01:55.949
"Okay"?

01:56.866 --> 01:57.867
That's it?

01:58.868 --> 02:00.745
"Okay"?

02:01.788 --> 02:02.789
"Okay"?

02:03.706 --> 02:05.750
How could you do this to us?

02:29.440 --> 02:31.151
I'm sorry, Ha-kyung.

02:32.485 --> 02:34.404
You're right. I'm an asshole.

03:02.265 --> 03:05.101
The value went up. It went up a lot more.

03:05.185 --> 03:08.062
The apartment was twice
as much as we'd paid for it.

03:09.814 --> 03:12.859
You know I don't have much money on hand.

03:12.942 --> 03:15.486
All of my savings went into that.

03:20.366 --> 03:21.409
That was your decision.

03:21.492 --> 03:24.621
Well, at first, my wife said
we don't need much,

03:24.704 --> 03:26.497
but that was before we got married.

03:26.581 --> 03:28.791
I'm 36. I'm an adult.
I need to provide for her.

03:28.875 --> 03:30.585
I'm entitled to something, aren't I?

03:33.588 --> 03:37.383
If it really means that much to you,
I'll be fair, halvsies.

03:37.467 --> 03:40.011
You should be so lucky. That's absurd.

03:40.094 --> 03:42.639
It makes sense.
I'm staying at Headquarters.

03:43.223 --> 03:44.224
Why should I care?

03:44.307 --> 03:47.143
Look, I don't want this to turn
into another big fight.

03:47.227 --> 03:48.436
But think about it.

03:48.519 --> 03:50.313
It's better for you
if we don't work together.

03:50.396 --> 03:51.689
Am I wrong?

03:59.364 --> 04:01.366
You can take your time and let me know.

04:04.452 --> 04:05.620
Hey, babe.

04:06.704 --> 04:10.250
No, I went to get you a treat. Macaroons.

04:11.084 --> 04:12.252
On my way back.

04:16.214 --> 04:19.342
You'll want to dress warm
if you're going outside this morning.

04:19.425 --> 04:22.345
The temperature in Gangwon Province
drops below zero.

04:22.428 --> 04:25.807
The temperature in the central region
is also below average for the season.

04:25.890 --> 04:28.601
The weather today
will start a bit like yesterday.

04:42.282 --> 04:44.284
Whether or not we consider
a temperature comfortable

04:44.367 --> 04:45.410
depends on the wind.

04:45.994 --> 04:48.955
The direction of the wind changes
whether we feel warm or cool.

04:49.038 --> 04:51.457
This holds true
even when we're in the same space,

04:51.541 --> 04:52.625
close together.

04:53.918 --> 04:56.379
Excuse me, sir.
Could you turn the heater off, please?

04:57.213 --> 05:00.550
Oh, it's too hot? It's strong, isn't it?

05:07.890 --> 05:09.851
Sir, could you turn on
the heater, please?

05:09.934 --> 05:10.852
It's freezing in here.

05:11.602 --> 05:12.520
Huh?

05:14.314 --> 05:15.857
Uh…

05:15.940 --> 05:16.899
Sure.

05:21.487 --> 05:22.822
Wind is unreliable.

05:23.406 --> 05:25.158
But the problem is, it's hard to see.

05:25.742 --> 05:27.410
Please, sir.
It's really too hot.

05:30.705 --> 05:31.581
Okay.

05:37.211 --> 05:38.463
It's too cold in here.

05:38.546 --> 05:39.672
Damn.

05:43.384 --> 05:47.638
Listen, can you two
just figure this out yourselves?

05:47.722 --> 05:49.349
Whether it stays on or off.

06:09.869 --> 06:16.459
EPISODE 2
SENSIBLE TEMPERATURE

06:24.884 --> 06:26.969
She said your ancestors saved you.

06:28.262 --> 06:30.348
Mom, did you see the fortune teller again?

06:30.431 --> 06:31.933
What else did she say?

06:32.016 --> 06:34.227
She said that one day,
you'll be over all this

06:34.310 --> 06:35.770
and be grateful to him,

06:35.853 --> 06:38.898
that you'll say, "Thanks for leaving.
You let me go like that."

06:38.981 --> 06:41.484
You're the one that seems grateful.

06:41.567 --> 06:44.028
I know you never liked him
as a future son-in-law,

06:44.112 --> 06:46.197
so you're relieved he broke it off.

06:46.280 --> 06:47.115
Yeah?

06:47.198 --> 06:49.409
Ha-kyung, our mom is still in shocked.

06:49.492 --> 06:51.702
I can't say it's not a little true.

06:54.122 --> 06:56.999
Your dad always wanted to get
to the end of the rainbow with business,

06:57.083 --> 06:57.959
and it was hard on us.

06:58.042 --> 06:59.544
He kept his promises, though.

07:00.420 --> 07:02.463
- Oh, Ma.
- I knew something wasn't right.

07:02.547 --> 07:05.550
Something was off with him
since I first met him.

07:05.633 --> 07:09.095
How can anyone in their right mind
back out of their own wedding

07:09.178 --> 07:10.555
only a month before?

07:10.638 --> 07:11.764
And what a cheapskate.

07:11.848 --> 07:14.642
I know it's normal for a couple
to split the bills these days,

07:14.725 --> 07:17.728
but I've never heard of another bride
who had to pay for so much,

07:17.812 --> 07:18.896
even her own wedding gifts.

07:18.980 --> 07:20.440
Wait. Did you look at my statement?

07:21.190 --> 07:22.358
I didn't even have to.

07:23.651 --> 07:25.486
We used my card, but he paid me back.

07:25.570 --> 07:26.654
Bunch of bull.

07:31.075 --> 07:33.202
Enough with the pity party.

07:33.286 --> 07:36.122
When you get the apartment,
make sure you get written proof for it.

07:36.205 --> 07:37.999
That's unnecessary. I own it.

07:38.082 --> 07:41.419
It's very important to get it written out,
or he'll say he's entitled to it.

07:41.502 --> 07:43.546
All right. Calm down, all right?
I'll handle it.

07:47.091 --> 07:49.218
You know that he said
she could have their place

07:49.302 --> 07:51.179
if he was ever to leave her alone.

07:51.262 --> 07:53.806
How can we trust him at all
when he's done worse for less?

08:01.189 --> 08:02.690
JIN HA-KYUNG
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

08:52.323 --> 08:55.284
YEOUIDO, SEOUL

08:55.368 --> 08:58.621
SENSIBLE TEMPERATURE 2°C

09:06.587 --> 09:09.382
- What did you say your name was?
- I'm Lee Si-woo.

09:11.384 --> 09:14.637
Well, I can't let you in
unless you got your station ID card.

09:14.720 --> 09:16.514
I work here, though. I can prove it.

09:17.348 --> 09:19.976
But I left both my ID card
and employee card at home.

09:22.270 --> 09:23.688
Where do I know him from?

09:25.147 --> 09:26.774
"Si" means time,
"Woo" means rain.

09:26.857 --> 09:29.527
"Rain that come on time." Lee Si-woo.

09:35.908 --> 09:37.618
Here, give me
your employee number.

09:38.494 --> 09:40.079
1835081.

09:40.162 --> 09:42.164
…5081.

09:47.336 --> 09:48.588
That's not you, though.

09:49.297 --> 09:50.798
Well, I…

09:51.799 --> 09:53.009
I used to be real chubby.

09:53.092 --> 09:55.219
You see, that's when I was studying
for the state exam.

09:55.970 --> 09:56.887
I don't know.

09:58.014 --> 10:00.516
- It's pretty different.
- It is me. I swear.

10:00.600 --> 10:02.727
See, if you look past the fat
here and here.

10:02.810 --> 10:03.978
It's how I look now.

10:04.937 --> 10:06.939
I can confirm that he's an employee.

10:07.023 --> 10:08.566
Oh, you know him?

10:08.649 --> 10:10.359
From the Metropolitan Office.

10:10.985 --> 10:12.236
Oh.

10:13.613 --> 10:15.906
Okay. You can… You can go in.

10:16.532 --> 10:19.201
But talk to HR, see if they can take
a new picture for you.

10:19.285 --> 10:21.412
Okay. Thank you. Goodbye.

10:24.707 --> 10:25.708
Hello again.

10:26.292 --> 10:28.336
Thanks again for helping out back there.

10:28.419 --> 10:30.880
- I appreciate it.
- And it's back to work.

10:44.644 --> 10:47.521
- Can I help you?
- Going to work, like you said.

10:49.231 --> 10:50.524
I just got reassigned.

10:50.608 --> 10:52.943
I'm on Severe Weather Forecaster,
Team Two.

10:53.027 --> 10:54.111
What was that?

10:54.195 --> 10:56.656
I'll be here, for two weeks.

11:08.709 --> 11:10.378
Has it been
seven years already?

11:10.461 --> 11:11.712
- Yes.
- Sir, I need to…

11:11.796 --> 11:13.673
- Yes?
- Oh.

11:14.715 --> 11:17.051
- Good morning.
- I'm glad that you're here.

11:17.802 --> 11:19.428
I wanted to introduce you.

11:19.512 --> 11:21.847
You probably heard from before
that this is Um from Gangneung.

11:21.931 --> 11:25.059
I brought him to be our new
Senior Forecaster on Chief Team Two.

11:26.018 --> 11:26.852
On my team?

11:27.728 --> 11:29.230
- So, Um?
- Yes?

11:29.313 --> 11:32.149
- It'll be great.
- Yeah. I'll do what I can.

11:32.900 --> 11:35.027
It was nice meeting you, Director Jin.

11:40.116 --> 11:41.325
Can we talk?

11:44.412 --> 11:45.454
Okay.

11:46.956 --> 11:49.500
You told me to think about it,
but you're forcing me out.

11:51.043 --> 11:52.253
You can stay.

11:53.462 --> 11:56.424
But I do need someone in line if you go.

11:56.507 --> 11:59.093
Soon, we'll have to prepare
for extreme summer weather.

11:59.176 --> 12:00.928
It'll be chaos without a director.

12:01.011 --> 12:02.972
And I can't just bring in someone
off the street.

12:04.098 --> 12:05.808
So I'm ready, just in case.

12:07.810 --> 12:11.272
Also, I know you'll go to Switzerland.
Isn't that why you came in?

12:11.355 --> 12:13.774
No, it's because
of the new severe weather forecaster.

12:14.358 --> 12:15.401
Ah, Lee Si-woo?

12:16.026 --> 12:18.404
That guy is looking for trouble.

12:18.487 --> 12:20.322
Well, first off, he's reckless

12:20.406 --> 12:22.158
and has no respect
for how things are done.

12:22.241 --> 12:24.827
- I know. He's impulsive.
- I'm concerned.

12:24.910 --> 12:27.204
He's got intuition. Like a super power.

12:27.288 --> 12:29.457
We could use
someone like that around here.

12:29.540 --> 12:32.126
Oh, I think he's more trouble
than he's worth.

12:32.209 --> 12:33.669
Please send him to the metro office.

12:36.297 --> 12:38.924
I don't know why you care
who's gonna be on your team

12:39.008 --> 12:41.469
- if you're leaving anyway.
- I never said I was leaving.

12:43.137 --> 12:44.305
So you're staying?

12:46.098 --> 12:49.018
Did they tell you
they cancelled my transfer?

12:49.810 --> 12:51.645
Well, I haven't decided yet.

12:54.398 --> 12:55.441
All right.

12:56.275 --> 12:57.443
You have a week. Okay?

12:58.068 --> 13:01.655
You must know how many people applied
to join WMO's program, right?

13:01.739 --> 13:03.866
I need an answer
for the International Division.

13:04.658 --> 13:05.659
One week.

13:06.786 --> 13:07.912
Understood, sir.

13:14.794 --> 13:16.962
- You were dispatched here?
- Uh, yeah.

13:17.046 --> 13:18.839
- For how long?
- Two weeks.

13:19.590 --> 13:20.925
- Huh?
- What?

13:21.675 --> 13:22.927
Hello there, sir.

13:24.178 --> 13:26.305
Hey, why aren't you
at the Metropolitan Office?

13:26.388 --> 13:27.431
Transfer.

13:28.098 --> 13:31.185
And, hey, why are you here?
You should be at the Gangwon Office.

13:32.019 --> 13:33.395
I've been transferred.

13:33.479 --> 13:34.897
- Oh!
- Really?

13:34.980 --> 13:36.607
Does that mean you're a director?

13:36.690 --> 13:38.567
I'm so happy for you.

13:38.651 --> 13:41.028
- I can't believe it took so long.
- Congrats.

13:41.612 --> 13:43.405
Not quite. Not yet.

13:43.989 --> 13:44.907
Which team are you on?

13:45.950 --> 13:48.452
Team Two. Team Two.

13:48.536 --> 13:49.995
- Huh?
- Team Two.

13:51.038 --> 13:52.164
Team Two?

13:53.040 --> 13:55.209
Is this desk okay
for the Senior Forecaster?

13:55.793 --> 13:57.753
Uh, hang on.

13:57.837 --> 14:00.881
You're here as a Senior Forecaster
for Team Two?

14:00.965 --> 14:02.383
Mm-hm. That's right.

14:02.883 --> 14:05.553
And you'll work for Jin Ha-kyung?

14:05.636 --> 14:06.637
Work?

14:07.680 --> 14:08.806
For her?

14:12.852 --> 14:16.230
NEWS
TRENDING SEARCHES

14:35.124 --> 14:36.917
You're losing your facial fat.

14:37.001 --> 14:38.210
It's 'cause you're married.

14:40.212 --> 14:42.172
Do you like it? Being married?

14:42.256 --> 14:44.008
How's Deputy Director Han?

14:44.091 --> 14:45.593
I know he seems he'd be cold and tough,

14:45.676 --> 14:47.344
but he's actually
really sensitive and kind.

14:47.428 --> 14:49.513
- Lucky.
- He likes to be helpful too.

14:49.597 --> 14:51.682
He does the chores and he's tidy.

14:51.765 --> 14:52.808
Oh!

14:53.559 --> 14:55.269
I thought he'd be really serious.

14:55.352 --> 14:58.188
Yu-jin, I swear you've been glowing
since the wedding.

14:58.272 --> 14:59.565
Lucky girl.

14:59.648 --> 15:00.733
You're so lucky.

15:21.295 --> 15:23.505
I feel left out.
I don't want to be single.

15:23.589 --> 15:25.257
I wanna get married now.

15:25.341 --> 15:27.176
I'd see it and I'd catch the bouquet.

15:27.259 --> 15:29.011
- Okay. Mm-hm.
- And then we'll glow too.

15:29.637 --> 15:30.763
I wanna be next.

15:31.764 --> 15:33.807
Okay, fingers crossed. Do it.

15:33.891 --> 15:35.893
But I have to find someone
who'll make me glow too.

15:37.436 --> 15:38.771
Why didn't I say hi?

15:38.854 --> 15:41.190
I made it weird. Why? What did I do?

15:41.273 --> 15:42.274
It's so sad.

15:42.358 --> 15:44.777
Well, that's what happens
if you date a co-worker.

15:44.860 --> 15:47.738
It's great if it actually last,
but you'll probably break up.

15:47.821 --> 15:49.323
It looks stupid for not knowing better.

15:49.406 --> 15:51.825
Well, she found Team Two,
and he's a spokesperson.

15:51.909 --> 15:54.078
It could be worse,
but they'll see each other…

15:54.161 --> 15:55.829
I'd be so sad I'd transfer.

16:00.167 --> 16:01.126
I would too.

16:03.587 --> 16:05.506
Hello.

16:22.815 --> 16:26.235
It can't be the Siberian air mass,
maybe if it was early in the year.

16:26.318 --> 16:29.488
Still, the Okhotsk Sea air mass
isn't strong enough

16:29.571 --> 16:31.073
to get this far to the west.

16:31.156 --> 16:32.741
Well, with the direction of the wind,

16:32.825 --> 16:34.702
it can only be coming
from the Okhotsk Sea.

16:34.785 --> 16:37.162
Look, maybe if it was born
from the northwest.

16:37.246 --> 16:39.999
Are you saying the sea alone
could drop the temperature this much?

16:40.082 --> 16:41.667
- No way!
- Well, it can't be from Siberian.

16:41.750 --> 16:42.668
What's happening?

16:42.751 --> 16:45.879
They're trying to figure out
why the temperature is going down.

16:45.963 --> 16:48.882
Senior Forecaster Um thinks
it's from the Siberian air mass,

16:48.966 --> 16:51.969
and Forecaster Lee thinks
it's because of the Okhotsk Sea.

16:52.636 --> 16:54.304
We're just scared to intervene.

16:54.388 --> 16:57.474
Neither thinks it's possible
for it to be the other air mass.

16:57.558 --> 16:59.184
It's from Siberian. It's Siberian.

16:59.268 --> 17:01.687
The Okhotsk Sea makes more sense
for the time of the year.

17:01.770 --> 17:04.690
Are you considering
the maritime polar air mass?

17:04.773 --> 17:06.692
- You might as well.
- What's that? Is that a joke?

17:06.775 --> 17:08.819
That's impossible.
That's a summertime air mass.

17:08.902 --> 17:10.571
Wouldn't you think
it's just that impossible

17:10.654 --> 17:12.656
that it's 5°C in May?

17:12.740 --> 17:14.908
You're right, but there's no way
it's the maritime polar.

17:14.992 --> 17:17.911
What I'm saying is we need
to consider every single option.

17:17.995 --> 17:19.288
Got it?

17:20.039 --> 17:21.040
Got it?

17:37.806 --> 17:40.225
Am I overreacting, or are you scared too?

17:40.309 --> 17:42.853
The Siberian air mass,
the Okhotsk Sea air mass,

17:42.936 --> 17:44.772
as well as the maritime polar air mass…

17:45.856 --> 17:47.733
And they have no idea what's going on.

17:48.776 --> 17:50.027
Another sign that it's the end.

17:50.903 --> 17:53.906
- You think they might lay everyone off?
- I'm not sure, but…

17:55.783 --> 17:57.951
I don't think Director Jin
will be here for much longer.

17:58.035 --> 17:59.244
- Why?
- Stop that.

18:00.037 --> 18:01.080
If she were,

18:01.872 --> 18:04.833
why would they have transferred Mr. Um
as a Senior Forecaster?

18:04.917 --> 18:08.462
Ah. Is she going to Switzerland?
Someone said that.

18:09.171 --> 18:11.131
It makes sense now.

18:11.215 --> 18:12.132
She'd go away?

18:12.216 --> 18:15.010
I heard his transfer was canceled.

18:15.094 --> 18:15.969
Oh, yeah?

18:17.513 --> 18:18.931
So she'd have to see him every day?

18:19.681 --> 18:22.434
That sucks. I'd be so uncomfortable.
Wouldn't you?

18:22.518 --> 18:23.644
For sure.

18:26.105 --> 18:28.440
So now she has to find a way out.

18:28.524 --> 18:30.818
That's so unfair. The woman always leaves.

18:30.901 --> 18:32.903
He should go.
He cheated with another woman.

18:33.570 --> 18:36.240
The world doesn't care
about who cheated or who didn't.

18:36.824 --> 18:39.451
It's all about who wants something more,
who has less dignity.

18:40.494 --> 18:44.289
I think she needs to fight a little more
before she goes to start fresh.

18:46.708 --> 18:49.503
Is Director Jin going somewhere?

18:53.215 --> 18:54.299
It doesn't affect you.

18:54.383 --> 18:57.886
Just do your job,
and go home in two weeks.

18:57.970 --> 18:58.929
Hang on.

19:01.640 --> 19:04.977
Hello. Team Two.
This is Oh Myung-ju speaking.

19:05.060 --> 19:06.311
Uh-huh. Yes.

19:40.929 --> 19:42.806
It's like a middle of winter over here.

19:42.890 --> 19:45.058
GANGWON REGIONAL OFFICE
OF METEOROLOGY

19:45.142 --> 19:47.769
Didn't you say the temperature
would warm up again in the evening?

19:47.853 --> 19:48.979
Yes.

19:49.062 --> 19:51.690
So, what's happening?
Why is it low?

19:51.773 --> 19:53.775
Based exclusively on the direction
of the wind,

19:53.859 --> 19:56.278
we could say the air mass
in the Okhotsk Sea is causing it.

19:56.361 --> 19:58.447
But we've yet to figure out
why the temperature dropped

19:58.530 --> 19:59.948
- in the first place.
- Really?

20:00.032 --> 20:01.533
What's the current sunlight?

20:01.617 --> 20:03.869
It's 73, similar to the average.

20:03.952 --> 20:05.787
That adds another piece of the puzzle.

20:06.371 --> 20:07.956
- Mr. Um?
- Yes?

20:08.040 --> 20:11.126
- What are your thoughts?
- Oh. Perhaps the remaining cold air

20:11.210 --> 20:14.254
in the northwest found a way to the west.

20:15.964 --> 20:18.091
Like in May of 1978?

20:18.675 --> 20:22.763
This phenomenon could be similar
to the drop we saw in April of 2010.

20:22.846 --> 20:26.308
We determined that the drop was due
to the cold air in the northwest.

20:26.975 --> 20:28.060
All right, but…

20:28.852 --> 20:30.938
what am I seeing over Okhotsk?

20:31.521 --> 20:32.481
We're looking into it.

20:34.775 --> 20:36.401
Of course, that's nothing new.

20:38.904 --> 20:41.114
Hm? What are your thoughts?

20:41.198 --> 20:43.450
Even if it's just personal opinion
or hunch,

20:43.533 --> 20:45.577
I think it's sea fog.

20:45.661 --> 20:48.497
It's coming when there's a temperature
difference between air and sea.

20:48.580 --> 20:50.457
The area is also known for it.

20:57.172 --> 20:58.382
Anyone else have an idea?

21:01.510 --> 21:03.345
All right. Here's the plan.

21:03.428 --> 21:05.639
We tell the media that this is temporary.

21:06.265 --> 21:09.268
Uh, I want you to go down
and explain it to them in person.

21:09.351 --> 21:10.269
Since it is strange…

21:14.856 --> 21:16.692
What? Is something wrong?

21:19.945 --> 21:22.322
- No, sir. It's a good idea.
- Okay.

21:22.406 --> 21:24.199
I'll go now and explain everything.

21:25.367 --> 21:26.285
Mm-hm.

21:26.868 --> 21:29.538
- All right. I'll check in later.
- Yes, sir.

21:29.621 --> 21:31.623
- Thank you, sir.
- Thank you.

21:31.707 --> 21:33.292
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

21:35.377 --> 21:37.421
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

21:48.473 --> 21:50.434
SIMULTANEOUSLY OCCURRING
COLD AND HOT TEMPERATURES IN MAY

21:54.813 --> 21:57.607
We believe the current weather
isn't as simple

21:57.691 --> 21:59.234
as a random irregular season.

21:59.318 --> 22:02.237
We believe it is a consequence
from worldwide climate change.

22:02.321 --> 22:04.281
To manage the mountain climate crisis,

22:04.364 --> 22:06.908
we'll strengthen the communication
and relationship

22:06.992 --> 22:09.953
between our departments in an effort
to protect all from extreme weather.

22:10.037 --> 22:12.164
He's good at navigating press.

22:12.247 --> 22:14.916
I think that's why
the Administrator thinks highly of him.

22:15.000 --> 22:16.668
And he wants him to stay close.

22:17.252 --> 22:18.628
He's good with words.

22:18.712 --> 22:20.005
Any questions?

22:21.006 --> 22:23.008
I'm Chae Yu-jin from Munmin Daily.

22:29.139 --> 22:31.475
How long do you anticipate
the cold is about to last?

22:31.558 --> 22:34.269
For that, I have to defer
to the Chief Forecaster.

22:40.984 --> 22:43.820
Currently, we see the cold spell
as a brief snap.

22:43.904 --> 22:46.615
It may be cold for another day
or perhaps for two.

22:46.698 --> 22:48.575
So it's gonna get warmer in two days?

22:49.368 --> 22:50.202
We hope so.

22:50.285 --> 22:51.661
According to the data, it's likely.

22:53.413 --> 22:56.792
Well, I hope your prediction is accurate.
I guess we'll see.

22:56.875 --> 22:59.503
Just in case, I'll keep my coat,
'cause you'll never know.

23:07.260 --> 23:10.389
If there are no more questions,
then this will conclude today's briefing.

23:10.472 --> 23:11.390
Thank you all.

23:15.644 --> 23:17.020
Yu-jin!

23:17.521 --> 23:19.064
Wait for me out there in ten.

23:20.690 --> 23:23.235
- Okay.
- Please follow up on that. Thanks.

23:25.487 --> 23:27.322
Congratulations, Director Jin.

23:32.661 --> 23:34.454
A little bird told me you were promoted.

23:35.163 --> 23:38.417
Wow, so you're the youngest director
in the history of the administration--

23:38.500 --> 23:40.168
Good work, Deputy Director Han.

23:41.128 --> 23:42.754
Have you thought more about the apartment?

23:43.380 --> 23:45.841
What? Why would I need to think about it?

23:46.758 --> 23:49.428
So, Ha-kyung, either way, you win.

23:49.511 --> 23:50.929
Even if we just go halvsies.

23:52.055 --> 23:53.265
But why?

23:53.348 --> 23:54.891
You really love going halvsies, huh?

23:57.727 --> 23:59.438
I wasn't gonna bring it up again, but…

24:00.689 --> 24:03.108
Can you tell me why you took the TV
if it's halvsies?

24:04.276 --> 24:05.444
I told you.

24:05.527 --> 24:07.362
I thought I could take whatever I needed.

24:07.446 --> 24:10.574
And come to think of it,
didn't I pay for the TV myself?

24:10.657 --> 24:12.576
No, you asked
that I'll pay for half of it.

24:12.659 --> 24:13.577
Did I?

24:16.663 --> 24:17.581
Oh.

24:18.081 --> 24:21.209
Did we use your card,
'cause I couldn't do it on my card?

24:21.293 --> 24:23.545
Yeah. I wired you 1,240,000 won.

24:23.628 --> 24:25.589
We paid in cash,
so they would install it for us

24:25.672 --> 24:27.674
and give us a toothbrush sterilizer.

24:29.217 --> 24:31.219
Right. I think I recall that.

24:31.303 --> 24:34.306
The TV, induction cooker,
and workout equipment are mine.

24:34.389 --> 24:36.808
If you don't give them back,
the apartment is not considered.

24:36.892 --> 24:38.602
Hey, Jin Ha-kyung, are you serious?

24:38.685 --> 24:40.395
Address me formally and lower your voice.

24:41.104 --> 24:43.273
- This is our workplace.
- Hey.

24:43.773 --> 24:45.233
I told you.

24:45.317 --> 24:47.986
Arguing with you at work
is my worst nightmare.

24:48.069 --> 24:50.113
But if this is how you're gonna be,
you leave me no choice.

24:50.197 --> 24:51.615
You know that's not true.
Do you wanna fight?

24:51.698 --> 24:52.949
- Do you wanna fight?
- Do you wanna fight?

24:53.033 --> 24:54.326
- No, I hate fighting.
- Same here.

24:54.409 --> 24:55.660
Director Jin,

24:55.744 --> 24:57.496
the Director General asked for you.

24:59.456 --> 25:01.833
I called you, but your phone
must be turned off.

25:01.917 --> 25:02.751
Oh.

25:05.045 --> 25:06.505
- Let's go.
- Bye.

25:24.523 --> 25:25.690
Hey, you.

25:31.947 --> 25:33.406
You know who I am, don't you?

25:33.490 --> 25:35.825
- Should I?
- You were at my wedding.

25:36.826 --> 25:38.036
Weren't you?

25:38.662 --> 25:40.539
- The bouquet.
- No.

25:43.208 --> 25:44.668
You must think I'm somebody else.

25:51.675 --> 25:53.426
Hey, is everything okay?

25:54.511 --> 25:57.305
Wasn't he that psycho
that tried to wreck the wedding?

25:57.389 --> 26:00.517
Who? That guy?
No, that's absolutely no way.

26:02.102 --> 26:03.311
Are you sure?

26:03.395 --> 26:05.564
Wouldn't that be wild?

26:05.647 --> 26:08.233
Mm. I've got to go.

26:09.109 --> 26:10.569
- See you back home.
- Mm-hm.

26:23.832 --> 26:25.041
Where are you going?

26:26.084 --> 26:28.253
I thought the Director General
wanted to see me.

26:28.336 --> 26:29.963
I might have made that up.

26:30.046 --> 26:31.840
It seemed like you needed an out.

26:32.507 --> 26:33.425
Ah.

26:34.301 --> 26:38.722
- Um, so, what was happening was--
- I didn't hear or see anything.

26:40.348 --> 26:42.100
That scares me more than saying you did.

26:43.935 --> 26:45.770
You should get some fresh air.

26:45.854 --> 26:47.147
I'm going back to the office.

27:10.420 --> 27:12.422
Can I talk to you in the parking lot?

27:46.247 --> 27:48.917
- What are you doing here?
- I work here like you.

27:49.000 --> 27:52.045
You're supposed to be working
at the Metropolitan Office.

27:52.128 --> 27:53.588
I got transferred.

27:54.631 --> 27:56.007
You just have to hurt me more?

27:56.091 --> 27:58.677
Humiliating me at my own wedding
wasn't enough for you?

27:58.760 --> 28:00.303
You followed me. So what's next for you?

28:00.887 --> 28:03.348
I didn't follow you here.
I'm only out here for two weeks.

28:08.144 --> 28:09.688
So can you keep it together?

28:10.313 --> 28:13.108
Is he gonna lose it if he sees us talking?

28:14.484 --> 28:15.443
I never told him.

28:19.280 --> 28:21.866
I never told him that we lived together.

28:23.201 --> 28:25.495
And I don't think
he'll ever need to know, either.

29:09.497 --> 29:12.125
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

29:16.588 --> 29:21.843
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

29:21.926 --> 29:24.387
- Hello.
- Goodbye.

29:25.930 --> 29:28.057
- Oh, hello.
- Hey.

29:28.141 --> 29:29.267
Hello.

29:32.103 --> 29:34.022
It's cold out there. Jeez.

29:35.190 --> 29:37.233
You think I don't know?

29:37.317 --> 29:41.112
Look at this. Hm?
The temperature's still going down.

29:42.280 --> 29:44.324
I don't think it's short-term, you know?

29:45.784 --> 29:47.952
- Hello.
- Hello.

29:48.036 --> 29:50.205
Hello. Gosh, it's cold.

29:51.456 --> 29:52.457
Oh.

29:53.541 --> 29:54.542
Hey.

29:55.293 --> 29:56.169
Um?

29:57.003 --> 29:58.838
How long has it been, huh?

29:58.922 --> 30:01.508
You see me on the screen every day,
so not that long.

30:01.591 --> 30:04.677
You look better on screen.

30:06.429 --> 30:07.722
I'll let you get back to it.

30:07.806 --> 30:08.640
Thanks.

30:09.557 --> 30:10.934
- Hello.
- Hello.

30:12.268 --> 30:13.478
Take a look at this.

30:46.261 --> 30:48.012
You wanna come get a drink with us?

30:48.096 --> 30:50.723
It's so lucky that we wound up here,
we should get to know you.

30:50.807 --> 30:52.183
Plus, you guys could chat.

30:53.434 --> 30:56.229
Uh, I have to check into my new place
by eight o'clock.

30:56.855 --> 30:57.856
Next time.

31:01.401 --> 31:02.861
I have to go as well.

31:02.944 --> 31:03.987
- Thanks, though.
- Bye.

31:04.070 --> 31:04.946
Goodbye.

31:07.323 --> 31:09.158
Well, I told you they'd say no.

31:10.493 --> 31:12.495
We all know
that acting like a team is key.

31:12.579 --> 31:15.039
It's just that Director Jin
and the new guys,

31:15.123 --> 31:17.375
they all wanna do things their own way.

31:27.844 --> 31:30.054
Oh, well, it will work out somehow.

31:30.763 --> 31:33.057
We have to focus on the team ourselves.

31:33.141 --> 31:34.809
- So, drinks?
- Mm-hm.

31:38.438 --> 31:40.607
- It's good?
- Mm, it is.

31:45.320 --> 31:46.154
Who's that?

31:46.905 --> 31:48.615
At this time at night, I don't know.

31:52.410 --> 31:54.787
- Who is it?
- It's me. Open up.

31:57.457 --> 31:58.625
Oh, it's freezing.

31:59.208 --> 32:01.377
It shouldn't be possible in May.

32:01.878 --> 32:03.546
So you're just here all of a sudden?

32:03.630 --> 32:05.173
I told you earlier.

32:05.256 --> 32:07.967
I texted you. I moved to Headquarters
and I'll be home.

32:08.051 --> 32:10.887
- You texted me?
- Oh, come on.

32:11.471 --> 32:12.388
Hello, sir.

32:12.472 --> 32:14.390
You're so tall now.

32:19.145 --> 32:20.647
I'm interrupting dinner?

32:21.272 --> 32:23.149
There's not enough. There's no rice left.

32:23.650 --> 32:26.277
That's okay. I ate at the office.

32:26.861 --> 32:28.905
Please, eat. Eat.

32:45.838 --> 32:47.423
They assigned you to Headquarters?

32:47.507 --> 32:50.093
Uh-huh, and I'll shift my stuff here.

32:50.593 --> 32:52.345
They should be here tomorrow.

32:52.428 --> 32:55.056
How could you just text
about something so important?

32:55.139 --> 32:57.767
Come on. You know I never liked any fuss.

32:57.850 --> 32:59.310
I…

32:59.394 --> 33:00.269
Gosh.

33:00.353 --> 33:02.939
You needed to have told me
all about this weeks ago.

33:03.022 --> 33:04.732
We don't have space
for your stuff right now.

33:06.025 --> 33:09.237
Well, there isn't… It's not a lot.

33:09.737 --> 33:11.030
It's just two bags.

33:11.114 --> 33:12.782
You're so inconsiderate.

33:40.601 --> 33:41.728
That's all, ma'am.

33:42.395 --> 33:44.355
- Thank you so much.
- Have a good day.

33:45.940 --> 33:46.941
You too. Thank you.

33:47.025 --> 33:48.026
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

33:55.575 --> 33:56.743
What is this?

34:01.581 --> 34:03.791
OFFICE OF SPOKESPERSON
HAN KI-JUN

34:03.875 --> 34:05.043
Get everything?

34:06.044 --> 34:08.421
I only took these stuff,
because I thought you wouldn't need it.

34:08.504 --> 34:10.423
You can check. Everything's there.

34:11.049 --> 34:13.676
Oh, please, I wouldn't I need it?
What a joke.

34:24.979 --> 34:26.147
Okay.

34:40.161 --> 34:41.579
NEIGHBORHOOD MARKET

34:41.662 --> 34:43.623
Brand-new TV for sale.

34:54.383 --> 34:55.927
Rice cooker for sale.

34:57.136 --> 34:59.430
Speaker for sale. Still in box. 

35:00.139 --> 35:02.266
Suitcases for sale. Unused.

35:20.326 --> 35:23.496
Are you sure we're doing right?
I think it's the bottom.

35:23.579 --> 35:24.831
Oh. Oh!

35:25.623 --> 35:27.333
Are you okay?

35:27.416 --> 35:28.626
- It's in your hair.
- Aw.

35:28.709 --> 35:30.002
Ow. Stop it.

35:33.089 --> 35:35.633
Hey, if you don't want to do it,
just say so.

35:35.716 --> 35:38.803
- I can't.
- Hey, stop. You're gonna crease it.

35:38.886 --> 35:40.346
It was expensive. Look.

35:40.429 --> 35:42.640
How am I supposed to fix this?

35:42.723 --> 35:44.976
- I think it's lunchtime.
- We're not done.

35:45.059 --> 35:46.561
I'm hungry.

36:15.464 --> 36:19.260
YOU RECEIVED A MESSAGE

36:25.892 --> 36:27.810
How much for the TV?

36:27.894 --> 36:29.395
Eight hundred thousand.

36:29.478 --> 36:31.939
What? How much did you pay for it?

36:33.399 --> 36:35.026
It was 2,480,000 won.

36:35.109 --> 36:37.069
I had it less than three months.

36:37.570 --> 36:40.656
- Where did you get it?
- Yongsan Electronics Market.

36:40.740 --> 36:43.367
- Come on. You're a scammer.
- What's he saying?

36:44.619 --> 36:46.787
Excuse me. How am I a scammer?

36:47.705 --> 36:49.957
That's an overseas
shipping serial number.

36:50.708 --> 36:51.542
Overseas?

36:51.626 --> 36:53.002
Overseas shipping?

37:12.396 --> 37:13.481
Didn't I pay for the TV myself?

37:13.564 --> 37:15.274
No, you asked
that I'll pay for half of it.

37:15.358 --> 37:18.444
- Did I?
- Yeah. I wired you 1,240,000 won.

37:18.527 --> 37:20.196
AMOUNT I WIRED = 1,240,000 WON

37:20.279 --> 37:21.155
But that's…

37:21.239 --> 37:22.949
No one's stupid enough
to fall for this.

37:23.032 --> 37:24.533
Your prices are ridiculous!

37:24.617 --> 37:27.203
Han Ki-jun, you asshole.

38:05.533 --> 38:06.826
No.

38:16.669 --> 38:17.962
You're here early.

38:19.213 --> 38:22.133
- So are you. Why?
- I just like to do work early.

38:25.011 --> 38:27.722
Ah, Headquarters are so different.

38:27.805 --> 38:29.932
The library's got to be twice as big.

38:33.811 --> 38:35.980
There's no way you'll finish that
before the meeting.

38:37.732 --> 38:40.526
Unless I help you.
I'll look through these.

38:41.777 --> 38:44.488
Please don't think you're obligated to.

38:45.323 --> 38:46.574
I know that.

38:47.241 --> 38:49.285
Honestly, the Director
didn't even force me to come.

38:49.910 --> 38:50.828
Why are you here?

38:50.911 --> 38:53.748
Wanted to check in, see how you're doing.

38:54.707 --> 38:56.000
Why me?

38:56.584 --> 38:58.044
Well, you two were

38:58.127 --> 39:01.047
all anyone could talk about
when you broke up, right?

39:02.465 --> 39:03.758
So I figure out

39:03.841 --> 39:06.635
that Han Ki-jun was the bastard
that stole my girlfriend,

39:06.719 --> 39:10.306
and that the woman
he was supposed to marry was you.

39:10.389 --> 39:11.557
And I wanted to see you.

39:14.685 --> 39:17.104
This is why you shouldn't date co-workers.

39:18.606 --> 39:20.900
Literally, everyone here knows
about our relationship,

39:20.983 --> 39:22.234
and how it broke down.

39:24.362 --> 39:26.614
What happened when you saw them in person?

39:26.697 --> 39:28.741
It wasn't as bad as I thought it'd be.

39:29.492 --> 39:31.369
- You thought Han Ki-jun--
- How I felt.

39:35.206 --> 39:38.000
I thought my heart would break when I saw.

39:38.084 --> 39:39.668
It actually made me feel better.

39:40.711 --> 39:43.297
Finding out what kind of man she fell for.

39:43.881 --> 39:45.091
It brought clarity.

39:45.174 --> 39:47.426
I get it. He's such a loser.

39:48.135 --> 39:49.845
Tell me how you really feel.

39:50.679 --> 39:52.556
I really feel like such an idiot, though.

39:52.640 --> 39:55.101
I was in denial
about who he was until he left.

39:59.563 --> 40:02.650
Switzerland. I hear you're heading out?

40:04.151 --> 40:05.361
Who told you that?

40:06.070 --> 40:09.031
Everyone keeps saying
it's a matter of time before you go.

40:10.282 --> 40:13.119
Honestly, I'm hoping they're all wrong.

40:15.955 --> 40:18.332
Please don't run
just to forget two losers.

40:25.714 --> 40:28.968
I don't need your counsel,
nor is it your concern.

40:29.677 --> 40:30.970
Like the wind,

40:31.720 --> 40:33.681
an affair might not be visible
in the beginning,

40:33.764 --> 40:35.558
but it will leave a mark
on you personally.

40:36.225 --> 40:38.060
Big or little.

40:58.414 --> 41:01.500
Wow. It's a beautiful morning.

41:10.092 --> 41:11.010
What?

41:12.511 --> 41:14.138
You smell that, don't you?

41:15.723 --> 41:17.683
I definitely smell ice in the air.

41:20.102 --> 41:21.270
You can smell ice?

41:22.938 --> 41:24.273
In the last cold wave,

41:24.356 --> 41:26.984
Siberia had it way worse
than we did, you know?

41:27.067 --> 41:29.695
Of course, the sea
was completely frozen over.

41:29.778 --> 41:33.240
What do you think…
happened to all that ice?

41:39.622 --> 41:40.789
Let's figure it out.

41:51.884 --> 41:54.470
NAMDAEMUN, SEOUL

41:54.553 --> 41:57.556
SENSIBLE TEMPERATURE 0°C

41:58.641 --> 42:00.768
The cold air
from the sea of Okhotsk

42:00.851 --> 42:02.853
and Sakhalin is flowing to the east.

42:03.979 --> 42:05.648
After examining it this morning,

42:05.731 --> 42:08.776
since it was clear
the sea of Okhotsk had not thawed yet

42:08.859 --> 42:10.444
and froze completely last winter,

42:10.528 --> 42:13.197
it's now chilling the air coming
from the north.

42:13.697 --> 42:16.951
Really? So you're saying
that's ice that's left over?

42:17.034 --> 42:18.327
We believe so, sir.

42:28.879 --> 42:30.839
So it wasn't sea fog.

42:30.923 --> 42:33.467
It makes sense
since the drop is so dramatic.

42:33.551 --> 42:35.928
- Oh, they did it.
- Oh, man.

42:41.892 --> 42:43.185
No wonder.

42:44.019 --> 42:45.896
What would you say
the water temperature is?

42:45.980 --> 42:48.190
The Kamchatka Peninsula is 5 to 8°C,

42:48.274 --> 42:50.609
and Sakhalin is 3 to 7°C.

42:50.693 --> 42:52.945
Amazing. That's unprecedented. Right?

42:53.445 --> 42:54.822
So what should we do?

42:54.905 --> 42:57.199
To start, we'll record this
as the most unprecedented

42:57.283 --> 42:59.952
and lowest temperature
in the weather observation for May.

43:00.035 --> 43:03.247
We should announce the prediction
that the weather in Taebaek and Bonghwa

43:03.330 --> 43:06.917
and Gyeongbuk down
to as much as .5 and 1.2°C respectively.

43:07.001 --> 43:09.211
Unprecedented and lowest. Hmm…

43:09.295 --> 43:11.130
- Okay. Let's do it.
- Yes, sir.

43:11.213 --> 43:12.256
Of course, it's ice.

43:12.339 --> 43:13.799
All right, going forward,

43:13.882 --> 43:16.468
I wanna know how long
this will last, approximately.

43:20.764 --> 43:22.099
Are you going to lunch?

43:23.058 --> 43:25.269
- What if I am?
- Then I'll go too.

43:26.937 --> 43:28.063
Uh, Mr. Lee.

43:28.772 --> 43:30.816
Go to the cafeteria
or should we treat ourselves?

43:31.692 --> 43:34.570
- You really knew it was ice?
- Huh?

43:36.071 --> 43:38.490
You smelled it. Ice in the air?

43:38.574 --> 43:41.785
How can you smell ice
all the way from the seas of Okhotsk?

43:41.869 --> 43:43.537
I wouldn't think that it's possible.

43:47.124 --> 43:48.751
I'm only human.

43:48.834 --> 43:50.127
How could I have smelled ice?

43:50.210 --> 43:52.921
I don't even think
a dog could from so far away.

43:54.048 --> 43:55.591
Then what were you saying earlier.

43:56.592 --> 43:59.219
I found out by reading in the library.

45:47.244 --> 45:48.454
You're here early.

45:50.038 --> 45:51.290
So are you. Why?

45:51.915 --> 45:53.917
I just like to do work early.

45:58.088 --> 46:00.299
You're more gullible than you look.

46:00.382 --> 46:01.675
- Tae-kyung.
- Ha-kyung.

46:01.759 --> 46:03.761
I thought you said
you'd take care of the apartment?

46:03.844 --> 46:04.678
Oh, what happened?

46:04.762 --> 46:07.264
A certified delivery receipt
came today for you.

46:07.347 --> 46:08.974
What? Is it that bad?

46:09.975 --> 46:12.227
Does Han Ki-jun think we can't see
what he's doing to you?

46:12.311 --> 46:13.645
He wants your apartment!

46:16.690 --> 46:18.817
And Ma has never been this mad before.

46:18.901 --> 46:20.194
She said she wants to find him

46:20.277 --> 46:21.945
and see if a beating
would set him straight.

46:22.029 --> 46:24.114
I'm trying to hold her back,
so she doesn't go crazy

46:24.198 --> 46:25.574
at your work, you know?

46:27.493 --> 46:29.411
Are you there?

46:29.495 --> 46:32.080
Hey, Ha-kyung. Ugh, shit.

46:44.259 --> 46:45.219
Han Ki-jun!

46:46.553 --> 46:47.596
Come here.

46:54.561 --> 46:55.938
She wants you to go.

47:06.657 --> 47:08.826
What the hell was that for?

47:11.537 --> 47:13.413
Listen. We're at work.

47:14.248 --> 47:15.666
You're worried about all the gossip?

47:15.749 --> 47:17.709
Then maybe you shouldn't be
messing with me.

47:17.793 --> 47:19.044
What did I do?

47:19.127 --> 47:20.879
You're making it look like
I owe you something.

47:20.963 --> 47:23.090
How dare you? After everything else.

47:23.173 --> 47:24.842
Or did you forget we were together?

47:24.925 --> 47:27.177
What happened is completely separate
from the apartment.

47:28.345 --> 47:30.013
You're not even sorry, are you?

47:30.681 --> 47:31.974
I said that I was.

47:32.057 --> 47:33.475
How many times do I have to say it?

47:33.559 --> 47:34.601
More than once.

47:35.894 --> 47:38.230
You said you're sorry once,
then you started to pack.

47:38.313 --> 47:39.898
I did say it, though.

47:43.193 --> 47:47.072
Yeah. After we've spent
ten years together.

47:47.155 --> 47:48.198
Ten years.

47:48.282 --> 47:50.450
Then you decided
you didn't want that anymore.

47:51.326 --> 47:54.454
So fine. You said you couldn't help it,
it was my fault, so…

47:54.955 --> 47:57.040
Even if that's so,
you could've really apologized

47:57.124 --> 47:59.084
instead of mumbling while you left.

47:59.167 --> 48:02.379
You're the one who said
I should consider the apartment alimony.

48:02.462 --> 48:05.632
Why? Because you wanted it
to be over ASAP, is that right?

48:08.093 --> 48:11.179
Anyway, I thought it was my fault.

48:11.263 --> 48:13.015
You were just reacting to the situation.

48:13.098 --> 48:14.892
I've been stressed
and too focused on work.

48:14.975 --> 48:16.351
It was my fault for not doing more.

48:16.435 --> 48:19.521
And if I paid more attention,
I would've seen how lonely you were.

48:19.605 --> 48:21.857
I thought that if I'd put more
into the relationship--

48:21.940 --> 48:24.192
- Why say it if we both know?
- We do?

48:25.485 --> 48:28.113
You're right. We spent ten years together.

48:28.614 --> 48:31.909
Do you have any idea for those ten years
how unhappy I was?

48:31.992 --> 48:34.411
You thought I was worthless,
because you outranked me.

48:34.494 --> 48:35.621
You'd always say,

48:35.704 --> 48:39.166
"Deputy Director Han, bring me water.
Coffee. Get me a snack."

48:39.249 --> 48:41.418
You thought I spent all my time
just waiting for you.

48:41.501 --> 48:43.211
And the wallpaper in the apartment.

48:43.295 --> 48:44.963
We could have just hired someone to do it,

48:45.047 --> 48:48.467
but you insist that we do it together,
and I missed my day at work.

48:48.550 --> 48:50.218
Do you remember how that ended?

48:50.302 --> 48:53.680
They called you into work,
so I had to do the rest of it alone.

48:54.932 --> 48:56.016
I…

48:56.099 --> 48:58.518
I was so exhausted at the end of the day.

48:59.227 --> 49:01.104
Then you should have said something to me!

49:01.188 --> 49:02.147
Say something?

49:02.648 --> 49:04.274
You would've sulked until I let it go.

49:05.609 --> 49:06.652
When I think about it now,

49:06.735 --> 49:08.612
how I felt like
I had to prove myself to you,

49:08.695 --> 49:10.447
I can't believe I accepted it.

49:10.530 --> 49:11.990
And you had no idea, did you?

49:17.412 --> 49:18.830
So that means that

49:19.957 --> 49:22.250
all those years meant nothing to you?

49:23.251 --> 49:24.461
Whatever.

49:25.253 --> 49:27.005
How much will you give me
for the apartment?

49:27.089 --> 49:29.132
You said it yourself,
do ten years mean nothing?

49:29.216 --> 49:32.094
It's selfish for you to keep it
to yourself, you know that.

49:36.223 --> 49:37.599
It's been sold.

49:38.767 --> 49:41.311
You sold it? Really?

49:41.395 --> 49:44.022
We signed a contract,
they'll pay by the end of the month.

49:44.731 --> 49:46.233
So how much am I getting from that?

49:46.900 --> 49:49.695
It cost us 20 million won,
and you deposited 5.

49:49.778 --> 49:51.321
I paid the rest on my own.

49:51.405 --> 49:55.075
But I also covered the deposit,
down payment, and the mortgage on my own.

49:55.742 --> 49:58.245
So… So what are we going to get?

49:58.328 --> 50:01.206
Could we say that you only own 7%?

50:02.374 --> 50:04.960
And then I have to deduct
all the money that you stole from me

50:05.043 --> 50:07.504
when you said I was paying half
for things you got overseas.

50:07.587 --> 50:08.714
Wire it to you.

50:08.797 --> 50:10.298
Wait, Ha-kyung, I--

50:10.382 --> 50:14.845
Halvsies? You must be joking.
That's low, even for you.

50:15.929 --> 50:18.557
You're moving.
You're going to Switzerland, aren't you?

50:18.640 --> 50:20.434
You can back out. Give it to me.
'Cause you don't need it.

50:20.517 --> 50:22.144
Who says I'm going to Switzerland?

50:22.227 --> 50:23.770
Everyone thought that…

50:24.396 --> 50:25.272
You're staying here?

50:25.355 --> 50:27.357
I'm the youngest director in history.

50:27.441 --> 50:28.400
Why will I leave that?

50:28.483 --> 50:30.736
Oh, won't you hate seeing me
like this every single day?

50:30.819 --> 50:32.571
Oh, is it hard for you to see me?

50:32.654 --> 50:34.406
It's sounds like
you're the one who should go.

50:34.489 --> 50:37.200
I think you should be in Geneva,
you asshole!

50:47.627 --> 50:49.588
I don't want to hear about this.

50:49.671 --> 50:50.922
Ever again.

50:57.637 --> 50:59.139
The show's over.

51:07.647 --> 51:08.899
Sir, Switzerland is off.

51:10.400 --> 51:12.444
Seriously? You're staying?

51:13.070 --> 51:15.405
Yes. I'm going to get
Chief Team Two into shape.

51:16.448 --> 51:18.492
Okay. Then let's celebrate.

51:18.575 --> 51:22.037
I'm sorry, I have to get home.
We have lots to do tomorrow. Thank you.

51:50.690 --> 51:51.942
Director Jin.

51:53.026 --> 51:55.320
- Can I help you?
- Do you wanna get a drink?

51:57.739 --> 52:00.117
I know a great spot,
and it's not too far from here.

52:11.670 --> 52:13.755
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

52:20.595 --> 52:21.513
Cheers.

52:25.851 --> 52:29.396
I'm not used to drinking
with other people around.

52:31.481 --> 52:32.399
Really?

52:34.359 --> 52:36.987
I know. You met him at a bar, didn't you?

52:37.863 --> 52:39.364
Is that what you think of me?

52:39.447 --> 52:41.533
We've been dating
since we were in college.

52:41.616 --> 52:43.743
Then we both got in to the same office.

52:43.827 --> 52:45.078
Oh.

52:45.162 --> 52:49.124
My co-workers who'd been there a while
said not to date any co-workers.

52:49.708 --> 52:52.085
So Ki-jun and I kept it a secret.

52:52.669 --> 52:54.379
But at the welcome party,

52:54.462 --> 52:58.091
I drank too much
and shouted at everyone that he was mine.

52:58.175 --> 53:00.385
The rest is history.

53:02.012 --> 53:04.431
- What about you?
- Huh?

53:04.514 --> 53:05.974
The bouquet, what happened?

53:07.017 --> 53:08.059
Oh.

53:09.686 --> 53:10.604
About that.

53:12.898 --> 53:14.274
Yeah. One last photo.

53:14.357 --> 53:15.859
Smile, everyone!

53:15.942 --> 53:19.738
All right. One, two, three.

53:20.906 --> 53:23.074
Next is the bouquet toss.

53:46.973 --> 53:48.558
And I ran as fast as I could.

53:48.642 --> 53:50.393
You got away with it?

53:50.977 --> 53:53.271
Well, if some guys are
out there stealing girlfriends,

53:53.355 --> 53:54.356
that was nothing.

53:55.106 --> 53:58.068
Oh, you're completely insane.
But I'll drink to that.

53:58.735 --> 53:59.819
Cheers!

54:06.493 --> 54:08.995
I'd say Yu-jin was my first real love.

54:09.955 --> 54:11.039
But you know what?

54:11.539 --> 54:14.042
After messing with her to get revenge,

54:14.626 --> 54:16.086
I'm letting her go.

54:18.838 --> 54:20.382
I got to tell you.

54:20.465 --> 54:23.551
Yu-jin's hands
are straight up cursed for real.

54:23.635 --> 54:25.011
Cursed?

54:25.095 --> 54:26.846
If she picked it, it's wrong.

54:26.930 --> 54:28.014
You know?

54:28.098 --> 54:31.226
So I was thinking that could be
the real reason

54:31.309 --> 54:32.560
she chose him over me.

54:33.186 --> 54:34.396
It may be.

54:34.980 --> 54:37.440
Han Ki-jun is really childlike.

54:37.524 --> 54:41.152
If he gets a cold,
he'll whine until the whole world knows.

54:41.236 --> 54:42.821
Maybe she's into that.

54:44.239 --> 54:45.532
I can take care of myself.

54:45.615 --> 54:47.117
He's an awful driver too.

54:47.200 --> 54:49.786
It took him, like, five tries
to get his license.

54:49.869 --> 54:51.121
I got it on my first try.

54:51.204 --> 54:53.415
Really? Here.

54:53.498 --> 54:54.958
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

54:58.586 --> 54:59.838
And he's self-obsessed.

54:59.921 --> 55:02.924
It'd take him an hour to get an outfit,
so he's always late.

55:03.008 --> 55:04.426
Oh, and he hates bugs.

55:04.509 --> 55:05.802
He can't handle spicy food.

55:06.344 --> 55:08.805
And of course, he is so, so cheap.

55:08.888 --> 55:11.850
You heard that, though,
him asking me how much money he'd get?

55:22.319 --> 55:25.363
What was it about him
that made you wanna marry him?

55:28.450 --> 55:29.659
Uh…

55:31.536 --> 55:34.122
Well… Hmm…

55:36.166 --> 55:38.251
I guess I didn't mind the bad stuff.

55:39.753 --> 55:43.298
I didn't care that he needed
to be babied when he got a cold.

55:45.425 --> 55:48.553
I liked that he was frugal,
'cause it made me feel safe.

55:49.179 --> 55:50.638
'Cause he was looking out for us.

55:53.350 --> 55:54.434
Most of all,

55:55.518 --> 55:58.271
he was extremely proud of me
on what I did.

56:02.650 --> 56:04.736
I guess I was wrong about all of that.

56:12.410 --> 56:14.662
At least I know who he really is now.

56:15.705 --> 56:17.999
- Oh, really?
- Wind.

56:18.708 --> 56:19.626
What?

56:19.709 --> 56:22.754
You said wind always leaves a mark
even if we don't see it right away.

56:23.797 --> 56:26.383
I couldn't see the wind
or what it was doing to me.

56:27.342 --> 56:30.261
Then recently, I did see, so I'm done.

56:33.014 --> 56:34.391
Thanks for all that.

56:38.019 --> 56:39.479
Just happy I can help.

56:46.694 --> 56:48.196
Isn't it warm in here?

56:49.280 --> 56:50.532
Yeah, you're right.

56:51.032 --> 56:53.660
It is warm in here.

56:53.743 --> 56:56.204
You… You're both too warm, you sure?

56:56.287 --> 56:57.664
Yes.

57:03.920 --> 57:06.339
- Should we get another bottle?
- I'd love to.

57:06.423 --> 57:08.091
Excuse me, can we get another?

57:08.174 --> 57:09.342
Of course.

57:11.428 --> 57:14.639
Ugh, I'll never date
a co-worker ever again.

57:14.722 --> 57:17.350
Really? "Never" is a strong word.

57:17.976 --> 57:22.439
I know. I'm never going to date
anyone I work with ever again.

57:23.982 --> 57:26.734
Thank you.

57:32.365 --> 57:34.409
You sure you didn't see
the signs of the ice?

57:34.993 --> 57:37.036
Even now, when I look, I just see fog.

57:38.246 --> 57:41.749
Director Jin and Si-woo,
they, they found it on their own.

57:41.833 --> 57:43.084
Noted.

57:44.335 --> 57:46.838
You act tough, but you're a tsundere,
soft on the inside.

57:46.921 --> 57:48.798
Well, I'll still beat you.

57:48.882 --> 57:51.050
Wait. I didn't see that. Give me a second.

57:51.551 --> 57:54.345
How did I miss that? Over.

57:57.098 --> 57:59.017
I don't get it. You're happy to lose?

57:59.642 --> 58:01.060
Huh?

58:01.144 --> 58:04.731
Not that, it's just, it's just that
Jin said she's going to stay for a while.

58:05.690 --> 58:08.943
And she wants to keep leading
and to run Team Two.

58:09.569 --> 58:11.738
Um, I see.

58:11.821 --> 58:14.032
Which is difficult.

58:14.616 --> 58:18.745
'Cause you'd have to wait longer
before I make you a director.

58:18.828 --> 58:23.208
I told you, I don't need to be a director,
that's not why I'm here, it's all right.

58:25.627 --> 58:28.046
Knowing Team Two,
you'll have your hands full.

58:35.094 --> 58:37.514
Darn it. I don't care.

59:24.102 --> 59:25.270
You awake?

59:57.218 --> 59:58.344
Sorry.

59:59.929 --> 01:00:00.763
What?

01:00:02.015 --> 01:00:05.101
I have to apologize
for what happened last night.

01:00:07.145 --> 01:00:10.064
I thought we were both on board.

01:00:13.067 --> 01:00:15.612
And it was good.

01:00:18.323 --> 01:00:20.033
- Have a good night.
- Goodbye.

01:00:20.617 --> 01:00:23.077
Hey, Si meaning time,
Woo meaning rain, you rock.

01:00:24.078 --> 01:00:25.288
For real?

01:00:25.371 --> 01:00:28.458
If me being so big,
you think can I kiss you?

01:00:32.003 --> 01:00:34.631
- You won't.
- I will. See?

01:01:31.896 --> 01:01:33.898
You're right. We're both adults, you know?

01:01:33.981 --> 01:01:34.982
That's true.

01:01:36.776 --> 01:01:38.361
So what happened,

01:01:39.278 --> 01:01:41.072
it was only a hookup.

01:01:41.155 --> 01:01:43.324
It shouldn't have happened, but it did.

01:01:43.408 --> 01:01:45.535
It's more like a natural disaster.

01:01:45.618 --> 01:01:48.579
Like when two air currents
that shouldn't meet, do,

01:01:48.663 --> 01:01:51.207
and wind up creating lightning, you know?

01:01:51.290 --> 01:01:52.333
Okay. So?

01:01:53.334 --> 01:01:55.128
I think we have to…

01:02:00.383 --> 01:02:01.759
We have to forget all this,

01:02:01.843 --> 01:02:03.928
and move on like adults.

01:02:06.889 --> 01:02:10.768
It makes sense that you're going back
to the Metropolitan Office next week.

01:02:10.852 --> 01:02:13.354
And I need to focus on managing Team Two.

01:02:13.438 --> 01:02:15.523
So I really don't need any distraction.

01:02:15.606 --> 01:02:17.942
I honestly don't have time
for anything else.

01:02:18.025 --> 01:02:19.527
And you're my co-worker.

01:02:19.610 --> 01:02:21.946
I can't do that. You understand, right?

01:02:22.029 --> 01:02:23.364
No, yeah, I do.

01:02:25.575 --> 01:02:27.618
Okay. Well, it's good that we agreed.

01:02:27.702 --> 01:02:29.245
Yeah.

01:02:29.328 --> 01:02:30.913
- Good work.
- Thanks.

01:02:35.585 --> 01:02:36.753
All right, then.

01:02:38.671 --> 01:02:39.964
By the way…

01:02:41.257 --> 01:02:42.341
I'm not leaving, either.

01:02:45.344 --> 01:02:46.304
Hm?

01:02:46.387 --> 01:02:50.349
They said I've been officially made part
of Team Two,

01:02:51.184 --> 01:02:52.810
and formally starts next week.

01:02:56.898 --> 01:02:57.940
What did you say?

01:02:58.524 --> 01:03:00.485
I'm with you, we're on the same team now.

01:03:09.410 --> 01:03:11.078
That won't make things difficult.

01:03:11.162 --> 01:03:14.290
And we'll move on, like adults.

01:03:16.417 --> 01:03:17.460
Okay.

01:03:41.359 --> 01:03:42.985
This is insane.

01:04:11.097 --> 01:04:13.808
Where is Director Jin?
Is she always this late?

01:04:16.227 --> 01:04:17.478
Satellite center…

01:04:18.229 --> 01:04:21.524
Please lift the fishing ban.
What are you doing?

01:04:21.607 --> 01:04:23.693
Ugh. We're doing our best
to keep you safe.

01:04:23.776 --> 01:04:25.486
When there's severe weather,

01:04:25.570 --> 01:04:28.447
if we mess it up, it leads to casualty,
don't you know that?

01:04:28.531 --> 01:04:30.491
You're drawing things out on purpose.

01:04:30.575 --> 01:04:32.535
You're letting your feelings
affect your judgement.

01:04:33.119 --> 01:04:36.372
Don't worry. I won't ask you out
just because we hooked up.

01:04:36.455 --> 01:04:38.124
- Cool.
- They're gonna see us!

01:04:39.000 --> 01:04:42.086
Oh, no. Why are you acting guilty
if there's nothing to hide?

01:04:43.421 --> 01:04:44.922
That was too close.

01:04:45.006 --> 01:04:46.799
Do you have feelings for me?
